{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:hgap-norm","A norm bound gives the real-part\ncriterion","<p><em> The complex norm bound implies the real-part bound\n(<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>21</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></math></span> absorbs the slack), so it\ncomposes through Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#thm:hgap-real\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:hgap-real\">9.4</a> to the same\ncertificate. Define </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtext>block norm condition</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">:⇔</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>X</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup><mtext> </mtext><mo>∧</mo></math></span></div>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">‖</mo></mrow><mtext> </mtext><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">‖</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>X</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This sufficient condition is\nunproved. Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtext>block norm condition</mtext><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟹</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>Irrational</mi></mrow><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">(</mo></mrow><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> proved in full, with no\nfurther gap, by chaining Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#thm:hgap-norm\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:hgap-norm\">9.6</a><span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></math></span>Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#thm:hgap-real\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:hgap-real\">9.4</a><span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></math></span> Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#catalogue:cert:a10\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#catalogue:cert:a10\">6.47</a>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:positivity-remaining-residue-inequality","","<p><em> For every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>&lt;</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Hence <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span> for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></math></span>.\nThe proof is genuinely uniform in <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span>: it rests on two facts proved for all\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>, namely <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, by a\ntwo-case structural split (divisor letter vs. foreign prime power), with\nabsolute constants <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></math></span> and no\nlookup table.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:proved-implications","The proved implications","<p><em> For\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></math></span> inside the sign corridor (<span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></math></span>), a\none-sided residue gap at precision <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span> (size condition <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></math></span> and <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>) already forces <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>.\nNo lower margin at all is demanded. The proof chain is complete: the\ntheorem holds for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></math></span>, and\n<em><span class=\"math inline\"><math><mtext>cofinal upper-endpoint condition</mtext></math></span> <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo></math></span>\nIrrational <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span></em> is\nproved.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:te-chain","Five sufficient conditions","<p><em>\nEach of the five conditions below suffices for irrationality; none of\nthem is proved. The first four imply the upper-endpoint condition; the\nfifth gives nonintegrality directly by the endpoint identity. These are\nnot asserted to form a linear hierarchy. Here <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and every condition quantifies\nover arbitrarily large exponents <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span>.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em><em>Adjacent-suffix band</em>: </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>∧</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∧</mo></math></span></div>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mtext>suffix residue</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> (a two-sided band on the adjacent-suffix\nresidue directly, one candidate depth <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span>).</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Odd-prefix interval at the prescribed depth</em>: at the\nprescribed odd depth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></math></span>, a\ntwo-sided band of half-width <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></math></span> on the half-word residue modulo\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>q</mi></msup></math></span>. The depth is fixed by <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span>; it cannot be chosen independently\nof <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Centred-residue bound at the prescribed depth</em>,\n<em>proved equivalent</em> to the previous one: </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Centred-residue bound at a variable depth</em>: the same\nmagnitude bound with the depth restriction relaxed from the prescribed\nvalue <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span> to any odd <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></math></span> satisfying the half-cell fit <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>q</mi></msup></math></span> and the positivity\nrange <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Terminal dominance</em>: under the same bounds as item 4,\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></math></span>. This\nis a different one-sided comparison, treated immediately\nbelow.</em></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>For the first four conditions, the relevant implications into the\nupper-endpoint condition are as follows: adjacent-suffix band <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></math></span> upper-endpoint condition; odd-prefix\ninterval at the prescribed depth <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></math></span> adjacent-suffix band; centred-residue\nbound at the prescribed depth <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇔</mo></math></span> odd-prefix interval at\nthe prescribed depth; centred-residue bound at a variable depth <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></math></span> adjacent-suffix band; centred-residue\nbound at the prescribed depth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></math></span>\ncentred-residue bound at a variable depth.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:proved-implication","The proved implication","<p><em> The\ndominance hypothesis at a single odd rank already excludes integrality\nof <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math></span>, and the terminal\ndominance condition implies <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:sufficient-extension","A sufficient extension","<p><em>\nEither of the following suffices: (i) the lower-escape branch cofinally,\nas displayed just above; or (ii) the two-sided magnitude form (item 4 of\nProposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:te-chain\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:te-chain\">9.14</a>),\nwhich asks only <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></math></span> and which the Lean source proves implies corridor\nescape via a clean sign split (positive branch escapes above the\nterminal letter, negative branch escapes below the directed bound),\nwithout prescribing the sign of the centred representative. Neither\nbranch is supplied by the conditional sign identity itself.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:separation-rational-approximation","","<p><em> Unconditionally, for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\" fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\" fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>&lt;</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></math></span> is an explicit finite\ncomputable rational block. For fixed <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span>, the error tends to zero as <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi></math></span> grows. In the quantified condition\nbelow, however, the depth is prescribed, so increasing <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi></math></span> is not a free way to satisfy the\nseparation hypothesis.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:short-window-examples-through-exponent","","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The single witness <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>93</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> works for every threshold\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn></math></span>. Its certificate is\nverified by exact integer arithmetic on the finite totient windows. This\nproves the displayed bounded statement. It does not construct witnesses\nfor unbounded thresholds; further finite checks would extend the\nverified range, not establish the universally quantified condition\nbelow.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:diagonal-certificate-table","","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>L</mi></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> at depths <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>\nrespectively, extended by separate computations to 28 historical values\nthrough <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></math></span>. The later aggregate\ntheorem closes every scale <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>82</mn></math></span>\nwith no holes. Each witness is checked by exact integer arithmetic on\ntwo finite totient windows. For example, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12252240</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>26</mn></math></span> use <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>26</mn></math></span>, not every totient between\nthe endpoints <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>12252241</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>24504506</mn></math></span>. These computations verify the\nlisted cases; they do not give a formula producing a certificate for\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:sufficient-extension-2","A sufficient extension","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>C</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>L</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This asks for a\ncertificate within a fixed additive constant of the necessary\nlogarithmic depth bound. The uniform constant is an additional\nrequirement, not a consequence of the finite data.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:one-common-certificate-sixteen-shifts","","<p><em> </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The basepoint <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>14</mn></math></span> and depth <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>9</mn></math></span> are common to all sixteen shifts.\nConsequently, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>r</mi></math></span> whenever <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>den</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∣</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nfor some integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>16</mn></math></span>. The exact computation uses\ntwo nine-term windows for each shift and reduces their discrepancy\nmodulo <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></math></span>. The earlier eight-shift\ncomputation uses basepoint <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>12</mn></math></span> and\ndepth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>16</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:simultaneous-certificates-unrestricted-depth","Simultaneous certificates with\nunrestricted depth","<p><em> The existence of a function <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span> such that </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>L</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> is\nequivalent to irrationality of <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span>.\nUnder irrationality, one can take <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span> has a suitable depth.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:fixed-farey-bound","","<p><em> If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is rational, its reduced denominator\nexceeds <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>7.963</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>964</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>664</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>670</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>137</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>532</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>335</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>577</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>487</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>583</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>105</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>. This is the finite denominator exclusion in the\ncorpus, logically independent of the certificate-supply\nreduction.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:sufficient-extension-3","A sufficient extension","<p><em>\nSuppose <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span> and, for\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi></math></span>, the <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> gap check excludes every rational\nof reduced denominator at most <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is irrational: any rational value of\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> would have a fixed finite\ndenominator, contradicted at a sufficiently large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi></math></span>. Only unbounded exclusion bounds along\na sequence of windows are needed for this argument. No equivalence with\na bound for the continued-fraction denominators of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is asserted; such a comparison would\nrequire its own proof connecting those convergents to the certified\nintervals.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:two-adic-congruence-that-does","","<p><em> The theorem is unconditional and\nholds for <em>every</em> <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi></math></span>. For every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span>, and every bound <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi></math></span>, there are primes <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span> with a length-<span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> zero prefix and a terminal\nhalf-modulus, giving </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≡</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"1em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Under eventual integrality this transfers\nto an integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>z</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></math></span> and <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>z</mi><mo>≡</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.444em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:sufficient-accumulated-residue-condition","A sufficient accumulated-residue\ncondition","<p><em> Suppose that for every integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> there are <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> such that </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≡</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"1em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>: these two inequalities\nimply <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and the\nfull quantified certificate condition applies. The half-modulus\ncondition here is imposed on the accumulated weighted sum <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, not on a single totient\ndifference. An unbounded set of triples with no control of the shift\ndoes not supply the displayed quantifiers. The required family remains\nunproved.</em></p>"]],"source":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.json?v=e6abdbcd8877"}
